# T-457: the relay role skips its host's proxy, as if it read no
# HTTPS_PROXY, and dials each target from its host directly, so a target
# that only the proxy reaches is the role's 502; the test of the CONNECT
# must fail with its words. Its first step is a name, which the role then
# asks its own resolver for (`target.invalid`, which has no address), so
# the plant opens no connection to any target.
ENTRY=T-457
GROUP=resume
EXPECT='the name goes to the proxy, which reached the target'
RUN='cargo test --locked -p podssh-relay --features serve,plain-ws --test relay_serve_contract -- a_target_goes_through_the_hosts_proxy'
